# `amd_dsl_census-gate.py --refresh`, which is its ONLY writer. One TAB-
# separated TRIPLE per line: the row NAME, the ORACLE's value, the PORT's.
# Loaded by path by the gate and committed BESIDE it, because a gate's
# declared divergences must live in git -- not in `gates/artifacts/`
# (`.gitignore`d, and where one `rm -rf` takes them) and not in the
# environment of whoever ran it last.
#
# 31 DIVERGENCES of 1178 ROWS. Each block is a CLASS, and each
# class says WHY the two sides differ. A pin without a reason is a
# weakened instrument; a divergence without a pin is a silent one.
#
# dsl.py blob at HEAD, at `ad117c928` and at the pin `ad117c928^`:
# `pin_drift_hold()` re-measures all three on every run.
# HEAD blob of tinygrad/renderer/amd/dsl.py when these rows were taken: 6526706b

# 9 CLASSES ARE RETIRED AND GONE, AND EVERY ONE OF THEIR ROWS IS EXACT NOW.
# THEY ARE NOT IN `CLASSES` ANY MORE: A CLASS WITH NO ROWS IS A CLAIM THAT HAS
# STOPPED BEING TRUE, AND `classes_hold()` FAILS A CLASS THAT HAS NONE. EACH
# STORY IS BELOW, WITH THE READING.

# MODMASK -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 16. **TWO DEFECTS, AND THE CLASS NAMED ONLY THE FIRST.** (i) Its own diagnosis --
#     "`mod_mask` never tests WHICH modifier is set" -- is RIGHT, confirmed against dsl.py's OWN
#     LOOP rather than against the oracle's helper: dsl.py:313-321 EXECUTED VERBATIM over the
#     three fixtures answers `neg=0 abs=0 opsel=0` (VOP2_ALL), `neg=1 abs=0 opsel=0`
#     (VOP2_NEG), `neg=0 abs=0 opsel=9` (VOP2_HI) -- three accumulators that are NOT equal --
#     and `mod_mask.one` asked only `is the value a Reg`. (ii) **THE SECOND DEFECT WAS IN THE
#     ROWS AND NOTHING NAMED IT:** all three mask families passed `1`, so `ab` and `hi` were
#     `src0` under two more names, where the census's convention is abs -> `src1` (bit 2) and
#     opsel -> `src2` (bit 4). **A CORRECT `mod_mask` WITH THE OLD BITS STILL DISAGREES ON ONE
#     ROW**: `modmask_hi_hi` reads 1 because VOP2_HI's `src0.hi` IS set. MEASURED by restoring
#     the old bits over the new def -- 1 row moves, 32 divergences.
#     THE FIX is `mod_hit`, a chain of `Bool.pick`s in `src_bit`'s own shape, selecting
#     `Ov.neg`/`Ov.ab`/`Ov.hi` by the mask being accumulated. `mod_neg`/`mod_ab`/`mod_hi` below
#     it ALREADY read those three predicates and nothing called them here. `MOD_NONE` is NOT a
#     fourth CPython mask: it is `vals['src0'] = ...` NOT BEING A LINE, which is what the four
#     register-named families (`modmask_{src0,src1,src2,vdst}_*`) ask, and why they answer 0.
#     **IT WAS NEVER AN ABSENCE BUG.** `Vf.has` IS `vals[name] is not None` and `mod_merge`
#     already took it -- see the retired `MOD_MERGE` below -- so the port can and does tell
#     "absent" from "0"; `(vals.get(k) or 0) | bits` was a DIFFERENT def's problem entirely.
#     **THE OTHER HALF OF THIS CLASS WAS FIXED EARLIER** -- `src_bit.vdst`'s
#     `String.eq("vdst","vdst")` tautology, whose three pins (`srcbit_sdst|op|nosuch`) were
#     DROPPED rather than moved.
#     16 ROWS, ALL 16 DISTINCT -- measured: 16 pin lines under 16 distinct names, and the 21
#     `modmask_*` census rows under 21 distinct names, none of them among this census's 14
#     known duplicates. The class was NEVER "16 rows and some of them are the same row".
#     **TWO OF dsl.py's THREE FLAGS ARE STILL UNMEASURED**, and this is measured rather than
#     asserted: deleting `mod_hit.ab` and deleting `mod_hit.opsel` each move ZERO of 1178 rows,
#     because no fixture here sets `Reg.abs_` and the opsel family asks about `src2`, which
#     `VOP2_FIELDS` has no field for. `mod_src0_ab` / `mod_src0_hi` exercise the flags through
#     `mod_ab`/`mod_hi` -- the same three predicates, a different row.

# TO_BYTES -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 1. `to_bytes_vop2` CLEARED, and it is the LAST row AMDWORD32 owned.
#     `to_bytes_f32i` and `to_bytes_f16i` were already EXACT -- `bytes_of` used to drop
#     `8 - sz*2` CHARACTERS FROM THE LEFT of a ten-character `0x%08x`, which is
#     big-endian AND keeps the `0x` AND cannot widen past four bytes. What was left was
#     THE WORD'S WIDTH: `Res` was `Res{v: U32, s: String}` and `bf_set.placed` shifted
#     with `U32.shln`, so every bit at index >= 32 was DISCARDED and a 42-bit VOP2 word
#     lost `sdst` [41:36] and `op_sel` [35:34]. MEASURED, CPython: `raw == 0x4814060a00`,
#     `bit_length() == 39`, `_base_size == 6`, `to_bytes == 000a06144800`. The port read
#     `000a06140000`. `Res` is now `Wrd{w: H.I64, s: String}`, `wplaced` is the one shift,
#     and `bytes_of` reaches the high limb: port `000a06144800`.
#     THE COMPANION HALF WAS THE ORACLE, not the port. Its `hex8` was
#     `f"{v & U32:#010x}"` -- CPython's own `#010x` with the port's truncation pasted
#     back onto it -- so `raw_vop2_all` read `|0x14060a00` on BOTH lanes where CPython's
#     word is `0x4814060a00`. THAT SHARED TRUNCATION IS WHY 1175 ROWS DID NOT CATCH IT:
#     the two lanes agreed and were both wrong, which is the one failure a byte-diff
#     census structurally cannot see.

# HI_BIT -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 12. IT WAS 12, AND **HALF OF THE CLASS WAS TWO DEFECTS**. (i) `vgpr_encode.hi`
#     read `fit(set, or(set, X, f), v, f)` -- it OR'd bit 7 in and THEN tested
#     `encoded >= 128`, and since ORing 0x80 into an eight-bit value always leaves it
#     >= 128, EVERY `.h` in an eight-bit field took dsl.py:196's refusal arm. dsl.py:194-197
#     tests `encoded` BEFORE the OR. The six `_256`/`_300` rows were CPython `128`/`172`
#     against the port's `0`. (ii) THE ROWS READ THE WRONG SLOT: `urow(..., Res.v(...))`
#     prints `Res.v`, which IS `0` for a `Bad`, so the six `_384`/`_511` rows CPython
#     REFUSES were ALSO `0` -- a RIGHT ANSWER FOR A WRONG REASON that read as
#     agreement.

# ABSENT_OPERAND -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 10. A DEFECT NOBODY COULD SEE BECAUSE IT WAS ZERO. `BitField.set` (:114) opens
#     `if val is None: val = self.default`, so an omitted operand is written at its
#     DEFAULT; `fld_encode` NEVER READ `Vf.has`. It did not have to, because every
#     fixture that omits an operand spells the omission `Ov.none()` and `Ov.none().off` is
#     0 -- and every default in that file ENCODES to 0. So a missing field and a zero
#     field were the same number.

# VDSTY_MSG -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 9. IT WAS NOT A DIFFERENT DEFECT FROM HI_BIT, IT WAS THE SAME ONE. `vdstyencneg_*`
#     read `Res.msg(...)` -- the refusal slot -- while the oracle read `enc`, the WHOLE
#     answer. Six rows were answers CPython gives that the port dropped. `enc_text` is the
#     port's `enc`. BOTH CLASSES WERE "THE ROW DID NOT READ WHAT THE CALL RETURNS".

# MOD_MERGE -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 10. **THE CAUSE WAS NEVER INSIDE `Bool.pick`.** `mod_merge` put an OUTER `Bool.pick`
#     around the answer with the literal `0` as its else arm, so it answered 0 for every
#     case worth encoding. CPython's `(vals.get(k) or 0) | bits` is
#     `has ? (given | bits) : bits`, because the `or 0` is inert once the left side is a
#     U32 (`0 | bits` IS `bits`). AND A SECOND, INDEPENDENT DEFECT WAS IN THE ROWS: the
#     middle digit of `modmerge_{given}_0_{bits}` IS `has` and is `0` in every one of those
#     rows on BOTH sides, because `vals` is a dict and a value is looked up BY NAME.

# WALK_IS_VALUES -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 1. **THE ORACLE WAS THE SIDE THAT WAS WRONG.** The port's `Vf` list carries each
#     value's own field, so the port's list order IS `dsl.py:334-335`'s `_fields` order;
#     `raw_ord_swap` walks a TRANSPOSED FIELD LIST. CPython cannot observe a value order at
#     all. MEASURED on two real `dsl.Inst` subclasses, `first` and `second` both at [7:0]:
#     `A(_fields=[first,second]).(first=11,second=22)._raw == 0x16`;
#     `B(_fields=[second,first]).(first=11,second=22)._raw == 0x0b`; kwargs order is
#     invisible.

# SLICE_UNSIGNED -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 1. `reg_slice.go` printed `U32.show(start)` where dsl.py:26 formats the SIGNED
#     `key.start`; `key_text` spells a U32's two's complement back, and now spells both
#     bounds.

# ALIGN_SHIFT -- 0 ROWS. IT WAS 18. EVERY ONE IS DROPPED, NOT MOVED: `al_shift_of` read `U32.sub(Fld.align(f), 1)`, so
#     for `_align = 4` it answered 3 where dsl.py:210/:211 shift by
#     `_align.bit_length() - 1 = 2`, and every `afdec_sr_*` came out DOUBLE. THE FILE
#     ALREADY SAID SO -- the note at dsl.bend reads "whose shift is
#     `_align.bit_length() - 1` ... NOT the alignment itself" -- and `ALIGN_SHIFT_2` /
#     `ALIGN_SHIFT_4` ARE THE CORRECT CONSTANTS. THEY WERE DEAD: `grep -c` answered 2,
#     their own two definitions and no call site.

